    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n713" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăd-augesco</span></b> ,
		ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. inch. n.</i> [ad, <i>intens.</i>],
				<i>to begin to increase</i> or <i>augment</i>, <i>to grow</i>, <i>to
				thrive</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">neque adaugescit quidquam neque deperit inde,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					2, 296</span></i>
			; so also Cic. <b>poet.</b> in Div. 1, 7 <i>fin.</i></div>
